    "solution": "<b>1. Percentage = Per Centum (प्रति 100):</b><br>• 100 में 60 marks $= 60\\%$ &nbsp;|&nbsp; 100 में 80 marks $= 80\\%$<br>• 200 में 130 marks $= 65\\%$ &nbsp;|&nbsp; 50 में 16 $= 32\\%$<br><br><b>2. % को Fraction में बदलना:</b><br>• $60\\% = \\frac{60}{100} = \\frac{3}{5}$ (मतलब 5 में 3 का होना)<br>• $25\\% = \\frac{25}{100} = \\frac{1}{4} \\Rightarrow 12.5\\% = \\frac{1}{8},\\ 37.5\\% = \\frac{3}{8},\\ 62.5\\% = \\frac{5}{8},\\ 87.5\\% = \\frac{7}{8}$<br>• $6.25\\% = \\frac{1}{16},\\ 18.75\\% = \\frac{3}{16},\\ 31.25\\% = \\frac{5}{16}$<br>• $14\\frac{2}{7}\\% = \\frac{100}{7}\\% = \\frac{100}{7 \\times 100} = \\frac{1}{7} = 14.28\\% \\Rightarrow 7\\frac{1}{7}\\% = \\frac{1}{14}$",
